I think we're losing the context of the original subject wherein a
hero gets one-shotted by a mumak.  My advice, FWIW, is that a speed 12
hero, who would likely die from the 4d12 and 2d6 attacks of a mumak,
is better off running to the stairs than trying to fight (melee or
projectile) a mumak.  Mumaks are speed 9, therefore they get 3 moves
for your 4.  In a vacuum with plenty of ammo, sure, have fun, kill it
with arrows or daggers.  You're a ranger with +2 racial arrows? Sure
you're probably fine.  But if you try and a yellow light steps in your
way, or oops! a magic trap, or the minetown watch is blocking the
corridor don't be surprised when you die.

I say it is "needless risk" because there's no need to fight a monster
when you can just leave it there.  Kill it later if necessary.  Why
rely on things going your way (or more accurately, staying _out_ of
your way while you dance)?  The list of things that could go wrong is
long.

